# Accepted-risk CVEs for this image, one per line:
#   CVE-ID exp:YYYY-MM-DD # reason
# `exp:` is a native Trivy feature - once the date passes, Trivy stops
# honoring the entry and the scan fails again, so these don't rot silently.
# Re-scan `mongo:8.0` before the expiry below; if upstream has rebuilt the
# tag with a patched Go toolchain/openssl, drop the corresponding lines
# instead of just pushing the date out.

# Bundled Go toolchain (go1.24.6) inside the mongo:8.0 image itself, not
